  <running_head>TRACT. II. CAP. XXVIII.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">commonefaciens. <i>Obsignantia signa</i> (Græcis</l>
    <l n="2">σφεγγίδες dicta) sunt, quæ signatum</l>
    <l n="3">non tantum indicant, sive præsens, sive</l>
    <l n="4">præteritum, sed etiam veritatem alicujus</l>
    <l n="5">roborant. Huc ergo pertinent <i>Sacramen-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>ta</i>, <i>Sigilla</i>, <i>Pignora</i>, <i>Arrha</i> &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">1ā. <i>Septimò</i>, Signum est vel <i>indicans</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>tantum</i>, quod &amp; <i>materiale</i> dicitur; Vel</l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>indicans</i> &amp; <i>repræsentans</i>, quod <i>formale</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">appellatur. Hujus generis sunt <i>imagines</i>,</l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>statuæ</i>, <i>picturæ</i>, <i>comœdia</i>, <i>notiones primæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">&amp; <i>secundæ</i>, <i>species intelligibiles</i> &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">11. Plures differentias signorum apud</l>
    <l n="14">Metaphysicos habere poteris, ut quod sit</l>
    <l n="15">vel <i>actuale</i> vel <i>potentiale</i> doctrinale, vel</l>
    <l n="16">non doctrinale; <i>Proprium</i> vel <i>improprium</i>;</l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Theoricum</i> &amp; <i>Practicum</i>; σημαντικὸν vel</l>
    <l n="18">μιλαδελικόν: Sed vel spuriæ, vel inutiles</l>
    <l n="19">sunt, vel ad superiores reduci possunt.</l>
    <l n="20">Atque <i>hæc de Signo</i> &amp; <i>Signato</i>.</l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="1" caput="29" para="true">CAP. XXIX.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DE.</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Mensurâ &amp; Mensurato.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">1. REstat inter appositionis species <i>Men-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>suratio</i>, quâ unum alterius magni-</l>
    <l n="26">tudinem, numerum, perfectionem aut du-</l>
    <l n="27">rationem mensurat: ubi mensurans dicitur</l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>mensura</i>, prout alterum <i>mensuratum</i>.</l>
    <l n="29" type="foot" para="true">2.</l>
